---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ProfileCard from "../components/ProfileCard.astro";
---
<Base title="Aditya Wagh">
  <section class="intro-section">
    <div class="mb-6 md:float-left md:mr-8 md:mb-3 md:mt-2">
      <ProfileCard />
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-5 text-pretty">
      <h1 class="text-center text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-balance">Aditya Wagh</h1>

      <p>
        Hi, I'm a software engineer based in London. I'm currently a <strong>Member of Technical Staff</strong> at
        <a href="https://neuracore.com">Neuracore</a>, where I work on building the infrastructure layer for the
        <strong>Physical AI lifecycle</strong>, spanning data collection and training all the way to inference and
        deployment on real robots.
      </p>

      <p>
        I did my master's at <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_University">NYU</a> and my bachelor's at
        <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BITS_Pilani">BITS Pilani</a>, both in electrical engineering, with a
        focus on machine learning, computer vision, and robotics. Before Neuracore, I worked on machine learning
        based <a href="https://github.com/adityamwagh/SuperSLAM">SLAM</a> at NYU's
        <a href="https://ai4ce.github.io/">AI4CE lab</a> under
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=YeG8ZM0AAAAJ">Dr. Chen Feng</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        I enjoy making things faster and simpler: profiling a service, finding the hot
        paths, cutting work off the critical path, and streamlining the workflows around it.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-2">
        <p>
          Lately I've been spending time <strong>learning about ML inference</strong>:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-fg">
          <li>graph compilation and kernel fusion</li>
          <li>quantization, pruning, and distillation</li>
          <li>KV caching, continuous batching, and speculative decoding</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p>
        When I'm not working, I'm usually reading about public policy, city planning, history, psychology, and
        philosophy, spending time cooking Indian food, enjoying F1, football, and house music, or walking through
        lively neighbourhoods looking for good coffee and great ramen. If any of this overlaps with what you're into,
        work or otherwise, I'd like to hear from you. Find me on
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/adityamwagh">LinkedIn</a>, by
        <a href="mailto:adityamwagh@outlook.com">email</a>, or on
        <a href="https://twitter.com/adityamwagh">X/Twitter</a> (open DMs).
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="clear-both"></div>
  </section>
</Base>
